  "summary": "Seven preprints show that rankings and contrasts in omics readouts depend on evaluation depth, scoring, compartment and composition, not only on the underlying biology.",
  "synthesis": "Most of these preprints show that quantitative omics inferences are conditional on the context in which they are evaluated. Proteomic co-abundance method rankings change with evaluation depth, and colorectal fibroblast-epithelial stress granule contrasts depend on scoring method and depth. Post-stroke efferocytosis transcript signals are bounded by cell composition and time rather than flux. Cochlear ageing shows weak systemic concordance and a distinct macrophage programme. Cortical GABAergic channel expression aligns with dendritic conductance load in a reinforcing direction. A cell-state-conditioned sequence model predicts responses to an unseen stimulus but not stimulus-dependent genetic effects. The ImmunoTwin study reports a replicated coupling of T-cell exhaustion and macrophage M1 programs under checkpoint blockade. Together these point to explicit reporting of depth, scoring and compartment.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
